WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:07.830
Continue working on your project or open the file named for-anim-paths if you need to catch up.

2
00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:11.949
Earlier you learned how to add vehicles and characters to the scene.

3
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:18.149
These elements were mostly stationary even though the characters had some simple idle animations to them.

4
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:26.260
If you wanted to make the characters walk about or vehicles drive by, you need to use Animation Paths tools.

5
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.960
Initialize them to populate in the dock.

6
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.240
When you expand the Paths panel on the right, you get four options.

7
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:43.240
Dedicated paths are available for characters, bicycles, and vehicles, and a custom path can be used for other objects.

8
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.600
Mostly all these tools work the same way with slide variations.

9
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:53.000
We'll start with character paths but first, we'll make sure the right container is active.

10
00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:57.890
In the scene graph, right-click the people container and set it current.

11
00:00:58.579 --> 00:01:01.679
In the Path panel, click on Character Path.

12
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.579
The pen icon is automatically activated.

13
00:01:06.719 --> 00:01:10.819
Draw a path by clicking a few points on the sidewalk or in front of the building.

14
00:01:11.829 --> 00:01:13.629
Right-click to end the command.

15
00:01:21.109 --> 00:01:47.579
You have options to adjust the density, and path width, sort the ethnicity and clothing, and reverse the motion.

16
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.500
Or stop the walk altogether and have them idle in place as if they were waiting in line.

17
00:02:03.739 --> 00:02:08.840
Once you're done with one path, you can create another one by revisiting the Populate panel.

18
00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:15.030
You can then create other paths for other groups of people.

19
00:02:25.639 --> 00:02:29.340
You can adjust the path by relocating its placed points.

20
00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:43.270
If you're having difficulty selecting a path in the viewport, you can also select it in the scene graph.

21
00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:53.210
Similarly, you can create animation paths for vehicles.

22
00:02:54.539 --> 00:02:57.740
Zoom back a bit to give yourself a wider view on the main street.

23
00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.560
Make sure the appropriate container is active before you start though.

24
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:11.409
And then in the Populate panel, choose Paths, Vehicle Path.

25
00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:16.210
Again, use the pen tool to draw a path down the middle of the road.

26
00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:38.060
Here you can choose options such as the number of lanes, or in this case, a two-way road.

27
00:03:39.750 --> 00:04:07.039
You can adjust the lane offset, vehicle density, and speed as well.

28
00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:20.860
If you were to reduce the speed and get closer to a car, you'll see the wheels rotating properly.

29
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.449
You don't have to adjust anything to get the proper behavior.

30
00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:39.350
Another nice touch is that if you were to use the time of day to switch to night time,

31
00:04:41.519 --> 00:04:43.819
then car lights are automatically activated.

32
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.800
You can press G to disable the helper's visibility in the viewport.

33
00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.389
The scene is coming together nicely.

34
00:04:51.389 --> 00:04:59.540
In the last video, we'll bring a bit more life to it by adding vegetation, like grass, shrubs, and trees.
